    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi echasnovski! I came across an issue with completion items listed in mini.completion and specifically java.\r\nHere is a screenshot of it\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed923ed7-44d5-4554-ab0c-43ccbb1931d7)\r\nThe thing is each completion item is very long for java setup using nvim-jdtls plugin which inturn makes the doc window not so good to read.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4e67c9f-8f07-4950-b834-0258d193eda7)\r\nSo I wanted to know if there is any way in mini.completion to remove the extra part of completion items after completion kind and probably add it in the doc window as a heading if possible in any way.\r\nIs something like this possible with mini.completion. I am currently struggling with this issue at work since the completion items itself cover most of the screen and the doc window is literally unreadable.\r\n\r\nDo you think you there is any workaround for this issue?\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi echasnovski! I came across an issue with completion items listed in mini.completion and specifically java.<br>\nHere is a screenshot of it<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/56352048/381196729-ed923ed7-44d5-4554-ab0c-43ccbb1931d7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..r3ywSzzdJt5WuzvWfrZnMJP0K6aePX5NwVEgSkeSCUQ\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/56352048/381196729-ed923ed7-44d5-4554-ab0c-43ccbb1931d7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..r3ywSzzdJt5WuzvWfrZnMJP0K6aePX5NwVEgSkeSCUQ\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a><br>\nThe thing is each completion item is very long for java setup using nvim-jdtls plugin which inturn makes the doc window not so good to read.<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/56352048/381198256-b4e67c9f-8f07-4950-b834-0258d193eda7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..QL9Z7pYOI-Ml3CUlVk4PGtxKdqrqGiWKspeOpr2A2Ew\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/56352048/381198256-b4e67c9f-8f07-4950-b834-0258d193eda7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..QL9Z7pYOI-Ml3CUlVk4PGtxKdqrqGiWKspeOpr2A2Ew\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a><br>\nSo I wanted to know if there is any way in mini.completion to remove the extra part of completion items after completion kind and probably add it in the doc window as a heading if possible in any way.<br>\nIs something like this possible with mini.completion. I am currently struggling with this issue at work since the completion items itself cover most of the screen and the doc window is literally unreadable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Do you think you there is any workaround for this issue?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi echasnovski! I came across an issue with completion items listed in mini.completion and specifically java.\nHere is a screenshot of it\n\nThe thing is each completion item is very long for java setup using nvim-jdtls plugin which inturn makes the doc window not so good to read.\n\nSo I wanted to know if there is any way in mini.completion to remove the extra part of completion items after completion kind and probably add it in the doc window as a heading if possible in any way.\nIs something like this possible with mini.completion. I am currently struggling with this issue at work since the completion items itself cover most of the screen and the doc window is literally unreadable.\nDo you think you there is any workaround for this issue?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-10-29T16:03:03Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "That part seems to be a `detail` field of what server returns and it is used as `menu` part of completion item.\r\n\r\nI think this will be resolved after #1258. In particular, see [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1258#issuecomment-2395393286).\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, you can use [`config.lsp_completion.process_items`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-completion.txt#L218) to modify items received from LSP server. I think something like this should be enough:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({\r\n  lsp_completion = {\r\n    process_items = function(items, base)\r\n      for _, i in ipairs(items) do\r\n        i.detail = nil\r\n      end\r\n      return MiniCompletion.default_process_items(items, base)\r\n    end\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs an alternative, you can also set `vim.b.minicompletion_config = { lsp_completion = { process_items = ... }  }` locally only for `java` buffers.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">That part seems to be a <code class=\"notranslate\">detail</code> field of what server returns and it is used as <code class=\"notranslate\">menu</code> part of completion item.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think this will be resolved after <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2567725836\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1258\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1258/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1258\">#1258</a>. In particular, see <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1258#issuecomment-2395393286\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1258/hovercard\">this comment</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In the meantime, you can use <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-completion.txt#L218\"><code class=\"notranslate\">config.lsp_completion.process_items</code></a> to modify items received from LSP server. I think something like this should be enough:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.completion').setup({\n  lsp_completion = {\n    process_items = function(items, base)\n      for _, i in ipairs(items) do\n        i.detail = nil\n      end\n      return MiniCompletion.default_process_items(items, base)\n    end\n  }\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.completion<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">lsp_completion</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">process_items</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">base</span>)\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">for</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">_</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">i</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">in</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">ipairs</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">do</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">i</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">detail</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">nil</span>\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n      <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniCompletion</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">default_process_items</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">items</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">base</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  }\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As an alternative, you can also set <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.minicompletion_config = { lsp_completion = { process_items = ... }  }</code> locally only for <code class=\"notranslate\">java</code> buffers.</p>",
            "bodyText": "That part seems to be a detail field of what server returns and it is used as menu part of completion item.\nI think this will be resolved after #1258. In particular, see this comment.\nIn the meantime, you can use config.lsp_completion.process_items to modify items received from LSP server. I think something like this should be enough:\nrequire('mini.completion').setup({\n  lsp_completion = {\n    process_items = function(items, base)\n      for _, i in ipairs(items) do\n        i.detail = nil\n      end\n      return MiniCompletion.default_process_items(items, base)\n    end\n  }\n})\nAs an alternative, you can also set vim.b.minicompletion_config = { lsp_completion = { process_items = ... }  } locally only for java buffers.",
